 "internal_silences": [],
 "text": "I learned to swim when I was thirty years old. As a child, I never had lessons, and I was always uneasy near deep water. One summer, I decided to change that. I joined a class for adults at the local pool. The teacher was patient, and the group was small. We started by simply floating and breathing slowly. After a few weeks, I could swim one length without stopping. By the end of the summer, I could swim for twenty minutes. It is never too late to learn a new skill. You only need to begin. Today, swimming is the way I relax after a long day at work."
